# The context for backend.e2e.Dockerfile, which is the distribution and the templates and nothing
# else. The repository's own .dockerignore excludes build/ outright, and rightly so: every other
# image compiles from source and must not be handed whatever the host had lying there. This one is
# the exception, so it carries its own list. BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore where it
# exists.
*
!build/install/ember
!templates
